uisr-s: sqrt(x) to the nearest integer, for x from 0 to 999.
Cells 79-98. To call it, load x into the accumulator and JMP 79.
It returns the nearest integer to sqrt(x) in the accumulator.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99.
Size 20 cells. It runs at most 302 instructions, 203.5 on average, counted from cell 79 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 79     696      STO 96   cells 79-81: the call: store x, and copy the return jump from cell 99 into cell 98
 80     199      CLA 99
 81     698      STO 98
 82     196      CLA 96   cells 82-85: x = x - 1, r = 0
 83     700      SUB 00
 84     696      STO 96
 85     796      SUB 96
 86     695      STO 95   cells 86-94: take 2r from x while that leaves 0 or more, counting r
 87     196      CLA 96
 88     795      SUB 95
 89     795      SUB 95
 90     397      TAC 97
 91     696      STO 96
 92     195      CLA 95
 93     200      ADD 00
 94     886      JMP 86
 95     000      data: the root r
 96     000      data: x, and then what is left
 97     195      CLA 95   cell 97: the root into the accumulator
 98     000               set on every call: the jump back to the caller
